~ diagrams are written as code in a raw @@diagram node. the default engine is
~ mermaid; (engine graphviz) selects another. wit emits the diagram into a
~ container that a mermaid-enabled page (or GitHub, for Markdown) renders to
~ SVG; a headless-browser build step can inline the SVG for self-contained
~ output.

@h2 A flowchart h2@

@@diagram
graph TD
  A[Write .wit] --> B[wit build]
  B --> C{Output?}
  C -->|html| D[MathML + diagrams]
  C -->|pdf| E[Paginated print]
diagram@@

@h2 A sequence diagram h2@

@@diagram
sequenceDiagram
  Author->>CLI: wit build report.wit
  CLI->>Renderer: expand + render
  Renderer-->>Author: report.html
diagram@@

~ the engine is selectable per diagram
@@diagram(engine graphviz) digraph { rankdir=LR; parse -> resolve -> expand -> render } diagram@@
